Insert Before Value X — Book Revision

To insert val before the node containing value X, first check if the list is empty. If head.data == X, create a new node, connect newNode.next = head, and return newNode because it becomes the new head. Otherwise, traverse the list using current until current.next contains X or current.next == null. If X is found, insert the new node between current and current.next using newNode.next = current.next and current.next = newNode. If X is not found, leave the list unchanged.

Time: O(n) — traverse the list in the worst case.
Auxiliary Space: O(1) — only pointers and one new node are used.

code
===============================================

/*
Definition of singly linked list:

class ListNode {
    public int data;
    public ListNode next;

    ListNode() {
        data = 0;
        next = null;
    }

    ListNode(int x) {
        data = x;
        next = null;
    }

    ListNode(int x, ListNode next) {
        data = x;
        this.next = next;
    }
}
*/

class Solution {
    public ListNode insertBeforeValueX(ListNode head, int X, int val) {

        // If the linked list is empty,
        // there is no node with value X to insert before.
        if (head == null) {
            return head;
        }

        // If X is present in the first node,
        // the new node becomes the new head.
        if (head.data == X) {
            ListNode newNode = new ListNode(val);

            // New node points to the old head
            newNode.next = head;

            // Return new node as the new head
            return newNode;
        }

        // Start traversal from the head
        ListNode current = head;

        // Move current until the next node contains X
        // or we reach the end of the list.
        while (current.next != null && current.next.data != X) {

            // Move current one node forward
            current = current.next;
        }

        // If X was found
        if (current.next != null) {

            // Create the new node
            ListNode newNode = new ListNode(val);

            // New node points to the node containing X
            newNode.next = current.next;

            // Current node now points to the new node
            current.next = newNode;
        }

        // Return the original head
        return head;
    }
}
